                <pb facs="0673" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/1172: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-25T12:00:00-05:00">April 25,
                    1929—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>137. Your 295, April 19, 6 p.m. Please telegraph what if any are the present
                    Chinese Government restrictions on importation of arms.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
